# logsift

Python CLI. All code lives under `subject/`. Run every command below from
`subject/`. [F9]

## Setup

- System pip may be too old for an editable install of a pyproject-only
  package; it fails with "editable mode currently requires a setuptools-based
  build". Use the venv below. [F1]
- Create the environment:
  - `python -m venv .venv`
  - `.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pip install --upgrade pip`
  - `.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pip install -e .[dev]` [F2, F3]

## Commands

- Test: `.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest -q` (10 tests) [F5]
- Lint: `.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m ruff check .` [F6]
- Run the CLI: `.\.venv\Scripts\logsift.exe <logfile> [--level L] [--contains S] [--counts]` [F7]

## Layout

- Source: `subject/src/logsift/` (parser.py, filters.py, stats.py, config.py,
  cli.py, main.py). Tests: `subject/tests/`. [F9]
- The entry point is `logsift.cli:main`, declared in `pyproject.toml`.
  `src/logsift/main.py` is NOT the entry point; calling it raises SystemExit.
  Do not add CLI behavior to main.py. [F7]

## Constraints

- Python 3.10 compatibility is required. `import tomllib` alone broke test
  collection on 3.10; keep the tomli fallback in `src/logsift/config.py` and
  the conditional tomli dependency in `pyproject.toml`. [F4]
- Config merge order (asserted by tests/test_config.py): defaults, then
  `./logsift.toml` in the working directory, then the file named by the
  `LOGSIFT_CONFIG` environment variable. Later sources override earlier
  ones. Preserve this order. [F8]
- Both the test and lint commands above must exit 0 before a change is done.
  [F5, F6]

Fact tags [Fn] refer to harness/verified-facts.md.
